WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.205
Book Two, Proposition One.

2
00:00:02.205 --> 00:00:16.896
If there be two segments, and one of them be cut into any number of segments whatever, the rectangle contained by the two segments is equal to the rectangles contained by the uncut segment and each of the segments.

3
00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:21.770
Let A and B C be two segments, and let B C be cut at random at D and E.

4
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:30.611
From B, draw B F at right angles to B C by One Eleven, and cut off B G equal to A by One Three.

5
00:00:30.611 --> 00:00:41.160
Through G, draw G H parallel to B C by One Thirty-One; and through D, E, and C, draw D K, E L, and C H parallel to B G.

6
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:47.622
Then the whole rectangle B H equals the sum of the rectangles B K, D L, and E H.

7
00:00:47.622 --> 00:00:55.250
Because B G equals A, B H is the rectangle contained by A and B C, and B K is contained by A and B D.

8
00:00:55.250 --> 00:01:04.161
By One Thirty-Four, opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal, so D K and E L each equal B G, and therefore equal A.

9
00:01:04.161 --> 00:01:10.505
Thus D L is the rectangle contained by A and D E, and E H is contained by A and E C.

10
00:01:10.505 --> 00:01:20.323
Therefore, the rectangle contained by A and B C equals the sum of the rectangles contained by A and B D, A and D E, and A and E C.

11
00:01:20.323 --> 00:01:22.060
Which was to be proved.

12
00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.155
Book Two opens Euclid's geometric algebra.

13
00:01:25.155 --> 00:01:37.320
Where modern algebra writes the distributive law—a times the sum of b, c, and d equals a b plus a c plus a d—Euclid proves it directly as an identity of area, free of numerical approximation.

14
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:50.440
In the GEOMETOR G-Index, node G eighty-two synthesizes seven foundational rules from Book One—perpendiculars, parallels, and parallelogram equality—with Book Two's first definition, the contained rectangle.

15
00:01:50.860 --> 00:02:05.641
You can explore the interactive diagram, trace the full dependency graph, and run the symbolic Python construction for Proposition Two One in the GEOMETOR Elements codex at geometor dot github dot i o slash elements.

16
00:02:05.641 --> 00:02:13.100
